{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "27", "m": "07", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "19", "M": "08", "S": "02"}}, "news": [{"title": "NGT directs verification of continuing 'illegal' construction in Greater Noida", "para": "The National Green Tribunal has directed the Uttar Pradesh Pollution Control Board to verify allegations. Some under-construction projects in Greater Noida allegedly continue despite closure orders for environmental violations. The tribunal is hearing a matter filed by BJP leader Rajendra Tyagi regarding these projects. The Greater Noida Industrial Development Authority is also examining details of these alleged violations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/ngt-directs-verification-of-continuing-illegal-construction-in-greater-noida/132665891?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1549826/132665891.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "SC asks Parsvnath Developers to file report on pending cases against it", "para": "The Supreme Court ordered Parsvnath Developers to submit a status report on pending cases.  The court also directed the firm to finish a homebuyer's dwelling unit within one week.  Parsvnath Developers had previously deposited the required amount with interest with the registry.  The bench warned of imprisonment if the company directors fail to comply with orders.  This action follows a prolonged struggle by senior citizens for their homes.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/sc-asks-parsvnath-developers-to-file-report-on-pending-cases-against-it/132665840?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-147362/132665840.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Mumbai: Pattathu Brothers' directors booked for failing to hand over amenities to housing society", "para": "According to a complaint lodged by an SRA assistant engineer, Joseph S Pattathu and Pearl Joseph Pattathu, directors of Pattathu Brothers, allegedly breached redevelopment terms by failing to transfer possession of six required facilities to the eligible beneficiaries after securing completion certificates for the project.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/mumbai-realty-firm-directors-charged-for-withholding-amenities-from-housing-society/132665807?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-651756/132665807.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}